    text check "9 + 16 = 25" #b5482e x 760 y 440 font_size 48 hidden true
    text tablet "Babylon, ~1800 BC" #2f6b8f cites ["p322"] x 760 y 330 font_size 34 hidden true
    text rope "3-4-5 = square corner" #2f6b8f x 760 y 250 font_size 30 hidden true
    path ga_v1 #8f887c points [[156,346],[156,478]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path ga_h1 #8f887c points [[68,390],[200,390]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path ga_v2 #8f887c points [[112,346],[112,478]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path ga_h2 #8f887c points [[68,434],[200,434]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gb_v1 #8f887c points [[244,346],[244,170]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gb_h1 #8f887c points [[200,302],[376,302]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gb_v2 #8f887c points [[288,346],[288,170]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gb_h2 #8f887c points [[200,258],[376,258]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gb_v3 #8f887c points [[332,346],[332,170]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gb_h3 #8f887c points [[200,214],[376,214]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gc_a1 #8f887c points [[235.2,451.6],[367.2,627.6]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gc_b1 #8f887c points [[226.4,513.2],[402.4,381.2]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gc_a2 #8f887c points [[270.4,425.2],[402.4,601.2]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gc_b2 #8f887c points [[252.8,548.4],[428.8,416.4]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gc_a3 #8f887c points [[305.6,398.8],[437.6,574.8]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gc_b3 #8f887c points [[279.2,583.6],[455.2,451.6]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gc_a4 #8f887c points [[340.8,372.4],[472.8,548.4]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    path gc_b4 #8f887c points [[305.6,618.8],[481.6,486.8]] style.stroke_width 1.5 hidden true
    group grid_a members ["ga_v1","ga_h1","ga_v2","ga_h2"] hidden true
    group grid_b members ["gb_v1","gb_h1","gb_v2","gb_h2","gb_v3","gb_h3"] hidden true
    group grid_c members ["gc_a1","gc_b1","gc_a2","gc_b2","gc_a3","gc_b3","gc_a4","gc_b4"] hidden true

    card title "What finishes Pythagoras' theorem?"

A right-angled triangle, with sides a, b and c: three, four and five. How are the three sides linked?
    draw tri rt la lb lc

Build a square on each side, and the answer is hiding in their areas.
    draw sq_a sq_b sq_c

    draw law

    ask "Which tile finishes the theorem, so that it holds for every right triangle?" on law others ["c","2c","(a+b)^2"] store t
        right: c squared: the two small squares together fill the big one.
        wrong: Look at what the squares measure: areas.

Check it here. The square on the short side holds nine little squares,
    draw grid_a n9

the one on the side of four holds sixteen,
    draw grid_b n16

and nine plus sixteen is twenty-five: exactly the big square.
    draw grid_c n25 check

It carries the name of Pythagoras, a Greek of about 500 BC. But a Babylonian clay tablet, Plimpton 322, lists such triples more than a thousand years earlier.
    draw tablet

And builders still use the trick: measure three along one wall and four along the other, and if the gap is five, the corner is square.
    draw rope

So the big square is the sum of the two small ones, on every right triangle there is.
    highlight sq_c
